# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Netlify redirects — processed top to bottom, first match wins.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Netlify's own address shows the same site; send it to the real domain so
# search engines index one copy. (Unique deploy links, <id>--...netlify.app,
# are other host names and keep working for previews.)
https://ubiquitous-cactus-9412cc.netlify.app/*  https://future-gen.co.il/:splat  301!

# English pages. An address with ?lang=en gets the pre-rendered English file
# (built by _tools/inject.py), so search engines and link previews read English
# without running JavaScript. Netlify's docs say the parameter list must match
# exactly, but on the live site (checked 3 Oct 2026) extra parameters such as
# ?lang=en&utm_source=... get the English file too. If that ever changes,
# main.js still switches the Hebrew file to English in the browser.
/                    lang=en  /index.en.html          200!
/index.html          lang=en  /index.en.html          200!
/syllabus            lang=en  /syllabus.en.html       200!
/syllabus.html       lang=en  /syllabus.en.html       200!
/accessibility       lang=en  /accessibility.en.html  200!
/about               lang=en  /about.en.html          200!
/about.html          lang=en  /about.en.html          200!
/games               lang=en  /games.en.html          200!
/games.html          lang=en  /games.en.html          200!
/accessibility.html  lang=en  /accessibility.en.html  200!

# Age-group landing links, e.g. for ads, an Instagram bio or WhatsApp.
# A 200 rewrite keeps the address (and any ?utm_... tags) intact;
# main.js reads the path and preselects the matching track.
# Netlify matches a rule with or without a trailing slash, so /10-12/ also
# lands here. (A "/10-12/ -> /10-12" redirect matched /10-12 itself and sent
# it in an endless loop; never add one.)
/10-12     /index.html    200
/13-16     /index.html    200
# At /10-12/ the page asks for its files under /10-12/ (assets/…): serve them
# from the root.
/10-12/*   /:splat        200
/13-16/*   /:splat        200

# Internal working files are not part of the public site.
/README.md      /404.html    404!
/_config.yml    /404.html    404!
/_archive/*     /404.html    404!
/_tools/*       /404.html    404!
